WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.503
-This will be cake compared to
what we did earlier.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.938
That was insane for me.

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.540
-It's so scary.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.209
I never thought that
I was a nervous person,

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:12.912
but it turns out I really am
because that is terrifying.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:16.916
-It's terrifying, and when you
feel heat coming off

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:20.586
of something, I knew it was
alive or something was there,

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:24.023
but then I go -- I thought
maybe it was our chemistry.

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.625
-Well, it could have been that
because it really got me going

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.461
when you were doing
that great little dance.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.931
[ Laughter ]
-That was a frightened dance.

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:34.267
I'm so happy you're here,
and I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.837
You know, the last time I saw
you, you were pregnant with

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:40.507
Harper, who is now 10 years old.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:42.542
-And you don't look a day older.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.476
-Yeah, right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.578
-You do not.
-Stop it.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.180
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.082
How is the family?
How is everybody?

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.883
-They're so good.
They're so good.

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:56.255
-Well, you, obviously, a global
superstar with Spice Girls.

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:57.524
You take Spice Girls.

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.793
You start your own fashion line.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.061
Again, global success. Congrats.

00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.095
-Thank you.

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.797
-That's a tough jump,
by the way.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:07.066
I know you were Posh
and everything, but still --

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:08.500
[ Laughter ]
-Do you know,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:10.970
I just feel so lucky
to have these creative outlets.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.171
You know, it's what
I love to do.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:15.174
I love fashion. I love beauty.

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.510
You know, I just love
to make women feel like

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.846
the best version of themselves,
and to be able to do that

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:22.047
through fashion --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:24.583
I do. I really, really do.

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:27.019
If somebody wants to
invest in my brand,

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.455
wear my clothes or my makeup,
that's why I'm doing it.

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.557
I want women to feel great
about themselves.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.592
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:36.830
-Do you remember the first time
you saw someone wearing

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:41.100
something from your line where
you're like, "Wow, I made that"?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.636
-Yeah, I think I was in
a restaurant with my husband.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:46.039
And I always like to compliment
women anyway, you know,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.774
even if they're not wearing
something of mine

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.142
just because I always think
that's really important.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.577
And I was just so excited.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:54.047
I mean, it's great seeing
anybody wear your clothes,

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.850
you know, not just celebrities
on the red carpet,

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.751
but anybody that wants to
wear my stuff.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:02.087
And it's very ex-- It's probably
really uncool actually.

00:02:02.087 --> 00:02:04.456
I really just want to clap
or something.

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.492
-Do you go around and just clap
and go, "I love it.

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:08.494
I'm so excited"?
-Yeah.

00:02:08.494 --> 00:02:10.429
-I have some photos
I want to show you,

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:14.733
because when you and
David Beckham started dating,

00:02:14.733 --> 00:02:17.002
you guys wore kind of
matching outfits a lot.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:18.637
I don't know if you did this
on purpose.

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:20.305
[ Laughter ]
Do you remember?

00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:23.176
I mean -- I mean -- Okay.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.011
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:27.680
-We have been known to. I mean,
we didn't do it that much.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.716
But every time we did,
it was very well-documented

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:33.052
and just will not leave me
alone, let me tell you.

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.954
-It follows you around, yeah.
-It really does.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:37.724
-But why did you do it? Because
you were just young and in love?

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.426
-It just seemed like a really
good idea at the time, you know?

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.660
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.128
-To wear matching outfits
together?

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:45.097
-It really did.

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:48.067
I think it was a naivete then.
We didn't know about fashion.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.503
We were just having fun with it,
which, to be honest with you,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.004
is kind of the way it should be.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.840
I really wish I had the courage
to do it more now.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:57.042
-Yeah. Do you feel like
that's been kind of

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:58.678
taken away a little bit
from you?

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.013
-I suppose the more that
you get to know the industry

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:04.083
and the older that you get,
you know, the less naive.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.485
I mean, we didn't know,
we didn't care.

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:06.852
We just had fun,
and we were like,

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:08.587
"Hey, let's wear
matching leather."

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.789
[ Laughter ]
And we did.

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:13.993
-Yeah, you definitely did.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:17.396
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh, they like it.

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:20.533
I think you should --

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:23.869
Just explain this situation.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:25.771
-You forget, right?

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:28.440
-I mean, you're both knockout,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.009
drop-dead-gorgeous-looking
people.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.810
So it doesn't matter what
you're really wearing.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.046
If I wore that,

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.182
I wouldn't look like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:39.051
-Well, we were actually
just on a country walk.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:43.255
And yeah.
-I want to go on a country walk.

00:03:43.255 --> 00:03:44.857
-You should try that outfit,
Jimmy.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.626
I think it could really work
on you.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.027
-But you've taken this now,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.563
and then you got into
Victoria Beckham Beauty.

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.898
-Yes.
-Which has also taken off.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:55.367
And I know,
from having interviewed people,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.736
how hard this business is,

00:03:57.736 --> 00:04:00.906
how many years go into
making something like this.

00:04:00.906 --> 00:04:04.110
It's very difficult
to take off and launch.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.644
And you did it. Congratulations.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:08.247
-Thank you. Yeah, it's been
a passion of mine and was

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:12.017
a big dream of mine to
really focus on clean beauty.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:15.655
So beauty formulas and packaging
that are clean,

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:18.391
but, you know, products that
are the ultimate in luxury

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:20.259
at an affordable luxury
price point,

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.761
products that really work,

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.864
products that I've never been
able to find in my makeup bag.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.900
And I'm a bit obsessed with
makeup.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.768
-You are, yeah?
-And also making sure

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:32.705
it's inclusive so that you can
find the perfect products

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:35.875
no matter what skin tone
you have, is really key.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:40.946
So, inclusivity, clean beauty,
but the ultimate in luxury.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:44.083
That was my goal,
and I saw a space in the market

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.452
where nobody else was doing
that, and it's going very well.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.553
-Good for you.
-Thank you.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.056
-And you did it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.258
I'm so happy to see you again.

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.626
Congrats on
your beautiful family.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.094
-Thank you so much.
-Best to everyone.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.629
Victoria Beckham, everyone.
-Thank you.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.665
-For more info on
her beauty line,

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.035
go to victoriabeckhambeauty.com.

